there are many things to redevelop it  because we are talking about a very  early stage field but if I could  highlight three the first one and very  important would be to bring government  to the table to the discussion why  because in Brazil most of the products  and services that are being developed by  entrepreneurs meet the public search  service to be incorporated for instance  we have new technologies that can really  improve education in our country but  they need to be incorporated by public  schools or we have new management tools  that could help public hospitals to be  much more efficient but they need to be  adapted and incorporated by municipal  and state governments so this is the  first important thing that I'm looking  forward to to help building in the next  couple of years the second one is to  develop new financial mechanisms for  early-stage businesses but not  mechanisms that are offered today to  businesses as usual we are talking about  a different model of business that need  more patient money that need more time  that needs some adjustments that need a  lot of dialogue between entrepreneurs  and investors so these kind of new and  innovative mechanisms for early-stage  businesses are very important to me to  be developed and the third one we need  more role models all businesses are in a  very early stage so what we really need  is models that can be consolidated that  can scale that can inspire intrapreneurs  and investors to take more risk to  really believe that it's possible to  combine profit generation with social  impact and to reach big social change
 

